sax: a LOK snapshot checks for input inside a long part

A snapshot save asks for waiting input as each OOXML part's serializer
opens. A part can be most of the export: a long document's
word/document.xml, a large sheet's XML. A key pressed while such a part
was written waited it out: 175 ms after the last check for a
12000-paragraph DOCX.
FastSaxSerializer now asks at every 512th element it starts. The stop
throws from the same serializer, as the check at a part's opening
does, so the exporters' guards cover it. Saves that are no snapshot
ask nothing.

--- a/sax/source/tools/fastserializer.cxx
+++ b/sax/source/tools/fastserializer.cxx
@@ -24,6 +24,7 @@
 #include <rtl/strbuf.hxx>
 #include <sal/log.hxx>
 #include <comphelper/processfactory.hxx>
+#include <comphelper/snapshot.hxx>
 
 #include <cassert>
 #include <optional>
@@ -337,8 +338,16 @@
     }
 #endif
 
+    void FastSaxSerializer::checkSnapshot()
+    {
+        // Ely: a long part stops for input too.
+        if ((++mnStarted & 511) == 0)
+            comphelper::LibreOfficeKit::checkSnapshot();
+    }
+
     void FastSaxSerializer::startFastElement( ::sal_Int32 Element, FastAttributeList const * pAttrList )
     {
+        checkSnapshot();
         if ( !mbMarkStackEmpty )
         {
             maCachedOutputStream.flush();
@@ -401,6 +410,7 @@
 
